J1 - Shared agent server spike: DONE

Measured RAM (win32, scripted fake model, offline, all 30/30 sessions fixed):

  BEFORE per-process (one heavyweight process per session)
    N=1  peak 409.5 MB   N=10 peak 1523.0 MB (marginal 123.7 MB/session)
                             N=30 peak 2476.7 MB (marginal  71.3 MB/session)

  AFTER  shared (one long-lived server hosting every session)
    N=1  peak 421.7 MB   N=10 peak  471.8 MB (marginal   5.6 MB/session)
                             N=30 peak  512.3 MB (marginal   3.1 MB/session)

Acceptance: bench/results/J1-before.json + J1-after.json committed (N=1/10/30);
shared marginal 3.1 MB/session at N=30 (< 10 MB target); all sessions fix the task;
launcher tests pass. The AFTER shape is landed as a selectable `code_session`
launcher (`launcher: "shared"`, default unchanged, opt-in via
LOAM_CODE_SESSION_LAUNCHER=shared).

Two measurement bugs were found and fixed, which is why these numbers supersede
the first committed run:
  1. Both shapes were measured in one process, so V8 grew the shared server's heap
     in response to the per-process run's ~2.5 GB pressure (shared N=30 read
     ~1500 MB instead of ~515 MB). Every measurement now runs in its own child
     process (runIsolatedMeasurement / --isolate <kind>, default on).
  2. --sample-ms (default 4000) capped the sampler, truncating the N=30 peak at
     1493 MB instead of the real 2477 MB. The window is now a backstop and sampling
     stops when the run's work is done.

